        "original_id": "c942b4bc-1d4c-5694-a363-cce2b4478de2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: A Leela of Her Own, Futurama, A League of Their Own\n- People: Hank Aaron, Bob Uecker, Tom Kenny\n- Organizations: Fox network, Atlanta Braves, Major League Baseball\n- Roles: right fielder, senior vice president\n\nFacts:\n- Hank Aaron was born on February 5, 1934, and his full name is Henry Louis Aaron.\n- Hank Aaron, nicknamed \"Hammer\" and \"Hammerin' Hank,\" is a retired American Major League Baseball right fielder.\n- Hank Aaron is the senior vice president of the Atlanta Braves.\n- \"A Leela of Her Own\" is the sixteenth episode of the third season of Futurama.\n- \"A Leela of Her Own\" is an homage to A League of Their Own.\n- \"A Leela of Her Own\" originally aired in the United States on the Fox network on April 7, 2002.\n- Bob Uecker voiced himself in \"A Leela of Her Own.\"\n- Tom Kenny voiced Abner Doubledeal in \"A Leela of Her Own.\"\n- Hank Aaron guest starred as himself and Hank Aaron XXIV in \"A Leela of Her Own.\"",
